# ChatRealty API — used SERVER-SIDE ONLY (never exposed to the browser).
# `create-chatrealty-site` writes your real values into .env.local for you.
# Get a token from Settings → Integrations on your ChatRealty site.
#
# RESTART THE DEV SERVER AFTER EVERY EDIT TO .env.local. Next reads this file
# once, at startup — not per request. A judged session set MARKET_CITIES to five
# cities, saw a sixth city on /listings anyway, and spent the session deciding
# whether the API filter was broken. The server had simply been running since
# before the edit. Ctrl-C, `npm run dev`, re-check.
#
# The token decides WHO the site is for and WHOSE CRM the leads land in. Confirm
# it is the right account (ChatRealty MCP → whoami) before you build.
CHATREALTY_API_TOKEN=crt_live_your_token_here
CHATREALTY_API_BASE=https://www.chatrealty.io

# Identity overrides (optional). The site's name, license, brokerage, bio and
# service areas normally come from the ChatRealty profile the token belongs to.
# Set any of these and that field wins instead — useful when you're building for
# someone other than the token holder, or when the interview turned up a license
# number or brokerage the profile doesn't have yet. Unset vars change nothing.
# AGENT_SERVICE_AREAS drives the /neighborhoods index, so set it for a
# single-market site whose token can see more than that market.
# Note: `set_site_live` checks the license on the ChatRealty PROFILE, so an
# override here shows on the site but does not unblock go-live.
#
# QUOTE ANY VALUE CONTAINING `#`. In a .env file `#` starts a comment, so
#   AGENT_LICENSE=CA DRE #02241837
# parses as "CA DRE " and the license NUMBER IS SILENTLY DROPPED — the footer
# renders "CA DRE" with nothing after it. That is a compliance failure (the
# license number is required IDX display content), and it fails quietly: no
# error, no warning, just a missing number. California's standard format always
# contains `#`, so this is the normal case, not an edge case. Use quotes:
#   AGENT_LICENSE="CA DRE #02241837"
# Same rule for any other value with a `#` in it (AGENT_TAGLINE, AGENT_BIO…).
# AGENT_NAME=
# AGENT_LICENSE="CA DRE #01234567"
# AGENT_BROKERAGE=
# AGENT_PHONE=
# AGENT_EMAIL=
# AGENT_WEBSITE=
# AGENT_HEADLINE=
# AGENT_TAGLINE=
# AGENT_BIO=
# AGENT_HEADSHOT=
# AGENT_SERVICE_AREAS=La Quinta,Palm Desert,Indian Wells
# AGENT_SPECIALIZATIONS=Luxury,Vacation rentals

# MARKET SCOPE — the cities the site browses when the visitor hasn't filtered.
# The feed is almost always wider than one agent's market (the shared dataset is
# statewide; a real MLS covers its whole association), so an unfiltered
# /listings served the entire feed: a Coachella Valley site opened on Oakland
# and Stockton homes. Unset, this falls back to AGENT_SERVICE_AREAS and then to
# the ChatRealty profile's service areas — set it explicitly when the browse
# should cover cities that aren't in the agent's service-area list.
# `off` (or `all`) disables scoping and browses the whole feed.
# MARKET_CITIES=Rancho Mirage,Indian Wells,Palm Desert

# CHAP — the on-site property chat. BYOK: any OpenAI-compatible provider.
# Groq (console.groq.com) is the recommended default. The widget hides itself
# until a key is set. SERVER-SIDE ONLY.
#
# NOTE THE NAME: the variable is CHAT_API_KEY, not GROQ_API_KEY — the site is
# provider-agnostic, so a Groq key (gsk_…) goes in CHAT_API_KEY. A judged
# session looked for GROQ_API_KEY, did not find it, and reported the chat as
# broken; the widget was correctly hidden because no key was set at all.
# CHAT_API_KEY=gsk_your_key_here
# CHAT_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# CHAT_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1

# Cloudflare Turnstile (optional) — bring your OWN keys to gate the inquiry
# form with a bot check. Get them at dash.cloudflare.com → Turnstile (free).
# Set BOTH to enable: the site key renders the widget, the secret verifies
# server-side in /api/lead. Leave unset and the form still has honeypot +
# rate-limit protection.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAA_your_site_key
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=0x4AAAAAAA_your_secret_key

# Auth.js — visitor sign-in. AUTH_SECRET is generated for you at scaffold time.
# Social login (optional): create YOUR OWN OAuth apps and the buttons appear
# automatically. Redirect URIs: {your-origin}/api/auth/callback/google and
# {your-origin}/api/auth/callback/facebook
# AUTH_SECRET=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# AUTH_FACEBOOK_ID=
# AUTH_FACEBOOK_SECRET=
